      "FacilityID": 1000122427,
      "SummaryText": "ONEOK Riptide Complex (Riptide, Phantom, War Horse and Shadowfax) is in Martine County,\nTexas, approximately five miles southwest of Lenorah, TX. Its coordinates are 32.24305\u00b0N, -\n101.90355\u00b0W. The address for the facility is 3014 FM 829, Lenorah, TX 79749. \nRiptide complex includes four non-fractionating NGL extraction plants: Riptide, Phantom. War Horse and Shadowfax. Riptide complex consist of inlet separation and filtration, amine gas treating and regeneration, glycol gas treating and regeneration, molecular sieve dehydration and regeneration, cryogenic processing units, refrigeration compressors, condensate stabilization, residue compression, hot oil systems, and all associated utilities and ancillary systems. Treated natural gas from residue compression are sent offsite via pipeline. Condensate recovered from extraction process is stored in Condensate Storage Tanks located in Riptide and Phantom Plants.\n\nRiptide Complex (or Facility) is subject to 40 CFR Part 68 because it consists of more than the\nthreshold quantity of a \u0093regulated flammable substance (10,000 pounds)\u0094. The total regulated\nflammable substance at the facility is 7,752,055 lbs. (including piping, 10% equipment inventory)\nplus 48,836 lbs. of methanol."
    }
